genre defying music embodiment of Jay-Z's influences ranging from Queen, Weezer, Prince all the way to De la Soul, Teddy Riley."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0334-d7da524aaa42:d02", "start": 0, "end": 107, "text": "Iconoclast (Symphony X album) Iconoclast is the eighth album by American progressive metal band Symphony X."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0334-d7da524aaa42:d02", "start": 108, "end": 221, "text": "It was released on June 17, 2011, in Europe, June 21, 2011, in the United States and on June 28, 2011, in Canada."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0334-d7da524aaa42:d02", "start": 222, "end": 444, "text": "When interviewed, vocalist Russell Allen said that the lyrical concept of the album is based on \"\"The idea of machines taking over everything, and all this technology we put our society into pretty much being our demise.\"\""}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0334-d7da524aaa42:d02", "start": 445, "end": 567, "text": "Allen said on Heavy Metal Thunder that \"it isn't a story, but rather a theme, like \"Dark Side of the Moon\" by Pink Floyd.\""}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0334-d7da524aaa42:d03", "start": 0, "end": 518, "text": "Heaven Shall Burn , a German extreme metal band Iconoclast trilogy , trilogy of Heaven Shall Burn productions Iconoclast ( Dope Knife album ) , 2014 album by Rap artist Dope Knife Iconoclast ( Nazxul album ) , 2009 studio album by Nazxul , an Australian black metal band Iconoclast ( Symphony X album ) , 2011 album by American progressive metal band Symphony X Iconoclast ( EP ) , 2014 EP by Clinton Sparks Songs [ edit ] `` Iconoclast '' , a song on Emerson , Lake and Palmer 's 1971 album Tarkus Other uses [ edit ]"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0334-d7da524aaa42:d04", "start": 0, "end": 229, "text": "Iconoclast: A Neuroscientist Reveals How to Think Differently Iconoclast: a Neuroscientist Reveals How to Think